  "content": {
    "id": "p2-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "Factorise the following.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p2-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x^2+6x+9$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x+3)^2$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2+6x+9&=x^2+2(x)(3)+3^2\\\\x^2+6x+9&=(x+3)^2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 11
      },
      {
        "id": "p2-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$x^2+2x-15$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x+5)(x-3)$",
          "worked": "$5+(-3)=2$ and $5(-3)=-15$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2+2x-15&=(x+5)(x-3)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 13
      },
      {
        "id": "p2-q2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$4x^2-8x-5$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(2x+1)(2x-5)$",
          "worked": "Split the middle term using $2+(-10)=-8$ and $2(-10)=4(-5)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}4x^2-8x-5&=4x^2+2x-10x-5\\\\4x^2-8x-5&=2x(2x+1)-5(2x+1)\\\\4x^2-8x-5&=(2x+1)(2x-5)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 17
      },
      {
        "id": "p2-q2-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$48x^2-27y^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3(4x+3y)(4x-3y)$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}48x^2-27y^2&=3(16x^2-9y^2)\\\\48x^2-27y^2&=3\\bigl((4x)^2-(3y)^2\\bigr)\\\\48x^2-27y^2&=3(4x+3y)(4x-3y)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 15
      },
      {
        "id": "p2-q2-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$25-(x+y)^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(5+x+y)(5-x-y)$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}25-(x+y)^2&=5^2-(x+y)^2\\\\25-(x+y)^2&=\\bigl(5+(x+y)\\bigr)\\bigl(5-(x+y)\\bigr)\\\\25-(x+y)^2&=(5+x+y)(5-x-y)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 15
      },
      {
        "id": "p2-q2-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$2x^2-7x-15$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(2x+3)(x-5)$",
          "worked": "Split the middle term using $3+(-10)=-7$ and $3(-10)=2(-15)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2x^2-7x-15&=2x^2+3x-10x-15\\\\2x^2-7x-15&=x(2x+3)-5(2x+3)\\\\2x^2-7x-15&=(2x+3)(x-5)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 17
      },
      {
        "id": "p2-q2-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$x^2-y^2+2x-2y$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x+y+2)(x-y)$\n\nUse the difference of two squares, then take out the common factor $x-y$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2-y^2+2x-2y&=(x^2-y^2)+2(x-y)\\\\x^2-y^2+2x-2y&=(x+y)(x-y)+2(x-y)\\\\x^2-y^2+2x-2y&=(x+y+2)(x-y)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 17
      },
      {
        "id": "p2-q2-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$(x-3)-x(3-x)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x-3)(1+x)$",
          "worked": "Use $3-x=-(x-3)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(x-3)-x(3-x)&=(x-3)+x(x-3)\\\\(x-3)-x(3-x)&=(x-3)(1+x)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p2-q2-i",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "i",
        "prompt": "$x^4-y^4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x^2+y^2)(x+y)(x-y)$\n\nApply the difference of two squares again to $x^2-y^2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^4-y^4&=(x^2)^2-(y^2)^2\\\\x^4-y^4&=(x^2+y^2)(x^2-y^2)\\\\x^4-y^4&=(x^2+y^2)(x+y)(x-y)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 15
      }
    ]
